+/// the raw L2 timestamp can resolve to an L1 block *after* the one the batch was posted
+/// in - and a forward-only scan started there would walk straight past the event and
+/// report "not finalized" for good. Backing the start off by an hour is well clear of that
+/// bound and costs at most ~300 L1 blocks, a fraction of the first 2000-block page.
